  "passage": {
    "text": "The price of milk is not always the same. Last month it was high, but this month it is lower. Why does it change? It depends on supply and demand. Supply is the amount of milk that farmers produce. Demand is the amount that consumers want to buy. When there is a lot of milk and few buyers, the price falls. When there is a shortage of milk, the price rises. Farmers cannot control the market price. This is difficult for them because their costs stay the same.",
